---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Card } from '@weluvabid/iris/components';
import { withBase } from '@lib/journal';
---

<BaseLayout title="About — Journal" description="How I approach software engineering and the things I like building.">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-muted-foreground">About</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
      I like finding out what happens underneath.
    </h1>

    <div class="prose-journal mt-8">
      <p>
        I'm Abid, a software engineer. I like pulling things apart to understand how they work. Sometimes
        that means reading through documentation or source code. Sometimes I end up building a smaller
        version myself because I want to understand the mechanics properly.
      </p>
      <p>
        That's led me through quite a few different problems: caches, serialization, storage engines,
        language tooling, reactive runtimes, browser extensions and frontend architecture. Some started
        with a practical problem. Others started with a question I couldn't leave alone. I enjoy both.
      </p>
      <p>
        I care about the details, but I don't think complicated code is automatically better code. I
        prefer implementations that are predictable, testable and easy to follow. I'd rather automate
        repetitive work than make every developer remember another step, and I'd rather measure a
        performance improvement than call something fast because it feels fast.
      </p>
      <p>
        I also enjoy the product side of engineering: understanding why something needs to exist,
        thinking through how people will use it and catching awkward edge cases before they become
        somebody else's problem. The implementation matters, but so does the thing we're actually
        building.
      </p>
      <p>
        Not every experiment needs to become a product. Some projects are useful tools; some are just
        me following an idea far enough to see where it goes. I contribute to open source for the same
        reason I build personal projects: there's always something interesting to learn by working on
        real code with real constraints.
      </p>
    </div>

    <Card.Root class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-border bg-muted/40">
      <Card.Header>
        <Card.Title>Have a look around</Card.Title>
        <Card.Description>
          The projects show what I've built. The writings show some of the thinking behind them.
        </Card.Description>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-5 gap-y-3 pt-3">
          <a class="text-sm font-medium underline underline-offset-4" href={withBase('/projects/')}>
            Projects
          </a>
          <a class="text-sm font-medium underline underline-offset-4" href={withBase('/journal/')}>
            Writings
          </a>
          <a
            class="text-sm font-medium underline underline-offset-4"
            href="https://github.com/weluvabid"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            GitHub profile <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </Card.Header>
    </Card.Root>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
